---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PortalCard from '../components/PortalCard.astro';
import { portalHref, portalLive } from '../config/portal.js';
---
<Layout
  title="Portal - Mt Cedar British International School"
  description="The Mt Cedar portal: sign in to sit an assessment, open your lessons, or reach the staff dashboard. Students sign in with a username and access code issued by the school."
  active="portal"
>

<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Mt Cedar Portal</p>
    <h1>One door to your work.</h1>
    <p>Assessments, lessons and results in one place. Students sign in with the username and access code issued by the school. There is no account to create and no password to forget.</p>
  </div>
</section>

{!portalLive && (
  <section class="slim notice-band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p><strong>The portal is being prepared.</strong> Logins are issued class by class. Your child’s teacher will send home a printed sheet with their username and access code before it opens, so nothing needs to be set up at home.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
)}

<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head"><p class="eyebrow">For Students</p><h2>Where do I go?</h2><p>The same username and access code work in both places. Keep the printed sheet somewhere safe.</p></div>
    <div class="feat-grid">
      <PortalCard
        title="Sit an assessment"
        href={portalHref('exam')}
        action="Go to assessments"
        meta="Username + access code"
      >
        <svg slot="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"><path d="M9 3h6a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v1H8V4a1 1 0 0 1 1-1Z"/><path d="M8 5H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v12a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V7a2 2 0 0 0-2-2h-2"/><path d="m9 13 2 2 4-4"/></svg>
        Objective questions are marked the moment you submit. Written answers are marked with AI assistance and checked by your teacher before the score counts.
      </PortalCard>

      <PortalCard
        title="Open my lessons"
        href={portalHref('lessons')}
        action="Go to lessons"
        meta="Works offline once opened"
      >
        <svg slot="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"><path d="M12 7c-1.8-1.3-4-2-6.5-2H3v13h2.5c2.5 0 4.7.7 6.5 2 1.8-1.3 4-2 6.5-2H21V5h-2.5C16 5 13.8 5.7 12 7Z"/><path d="M12 7v13"/></svg>
        Lesson summaries and practice questions your teachers publish. Once a lesson has loaded it stays readable without data, so it works on the way home.
      </PortalCard>

      <PortalCard
        title="Check a result"
        href={portalHref('results')}
        action="Look up a result"
        meta="Released term by term"
      >
        <svg slot="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"><path d="M14 3H7a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v14a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h10a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8Z"/><path d="M14 3v5h5"/><path d="M9 13h6M9 17h4"/></svg>
        Term result sheets are prepared by the school and released after each term. Until online lookup opens, sheets are issued directly by the school office. See <a href="/portal/help#results">how results are issued</a>.
      </PortalCard>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section style="background:var(--ivory-2)">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head"><p class="eyebrow">For Staff</p><h2>Teachers and administrators.</h2><p>Staff sign in with an email address and password, not an access code.</p></div>
    <div class="feat-grid two">
      <PortalCard
        title="Assessments &amp; results dashboard"
        href={portalHref('staffResultPeak')}
        action="Staff sign in"
        meta="Tutors and school administrators"
      >
        <svg slot="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"><rect x="3" y="3" width="7" height="9" rx="1.5"/><rect x="14" y="3" width="7" height="5" rx="1.5"/><rect x="14" y="12" width="7" height="9" rx="1.5"/><rect x="3" y="16" width="7" height="5" rx="1.5"/></svg>
        Build exams, review AI-marked written answers, manage your class roster and produce the term result sheets.
      </PortalCard>

      <PortalCard
        title="Lesson authoring"
        href={portalHref('staffLearn')}
        action="Tutor sign in"
        meta="Draft, review, publish"
      >
        <svg slot="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"><path d="M4 21v-3.5L15.5 6a2.1 2.1 0 0 1 3 3L7 20.5 3.5 21Z"/><path d="M14 7.5 17.5 11"/></svg>
        Upload a lesson and get a student summary, practice questions and a marking guide back. Nothing reaches students until you have edited and published it.
      </PortalCard>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head"><p class="eyebrow">Signing In</p><h2>Three things, in order.</h2><p>Designed to work on a shared phone with a weak signal: no app to install, no email address required.</p></div>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step">
        <h3>Get the sheet</h3>
        <p>The class teacher issues a printed sheet listing each child’s username and six-character access code. It comes from the school, never by text message.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <h3>Pick the right door</h3>
        <p>Assessments and lessons are two different places, but they take the same two details. Choose from the cards above.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <h3>Type the two details</h3>
        <p>Username like <code>jss3-04</code>, then the access code. The school is already selected for you.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="cta" style="margin-top:2.4rem">
      <a class="btn btn-cedar" href="/portal/help">Read the full sign-in guide <span class="arr">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--gold-bright)">Need a hand?</p>
    <h2>Lost a code? Ask the school.</h2>
    <p>Access codes are issued and reset by the school office. For your child’s safety we cannot send one over the phone without confirming who you are. Come in, or call and we will arrange it.</p>
    <div class="cta">
      <a class="btn btn-gold btn-lg" href="/contact">Contact the School <span class="arr">→</span></a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href="/portal/help">Sign-in Guide</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

</Layout>

<style>
  .notice-band {
    background: rgba(195, 150, 48, 0.14);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .notice-band p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink);
    max-width: 78ch;
  }
  code {
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    background: rgba(18, 60, 40, 0.08);
    border-radius: 5px;
    padding: 0.1rem 0.35rem;
    font-size: 0.94em;
  }
</style>
